Test connectivity from application-eks to monitoring eks network load balancer:
===============================================================================

switch to application eks cluster
$ kubectl config use-context application-eks
Switched to context "application-eks".

$ kubectl run network-test \
  --image=curlimages/curl:8.10.1 \
  --restart=Never \
  --rm -it \
  -- sh
and run below 3 command to check whethere we are able to reach from monitoring eks cluster

curl -I http://k8s-monitori-promethe-e0617ba28f-d5c130e99c27d8ba.elb.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com:9090/-/ready
curl -s http://k8s-monitori-lokiinge-a09257c812-8872d6d59604b187.elb.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com:3100/ready
nc -vz -w 5 k8s-monitori-tempoing-55de63d743-8734675630922384.elb.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com 4317


Application EKS
     │
     │ VPC Peering
     ▼
Monitoring EKS
     │
     ├── Prometheus NLB :9090  ✅
     │
     ├── Loki NLB :3100       ✅
     │
     └── Tempo NLB
          ├── :4317 OTLP gRPC
          └── :4318 OTLP HTTP
Do not add port 3200 to the NLB. 3200 is useful for Tempo's HTTP/query API, but Alloy only needs 4317/4318 for trace ingestion.
